# Fast intent heuristics (pipe-1.2.3 / acc-3.14)

**Read:** [docs/FAST_INTENT_HEURISTICS_BOUNDARY.md](../../docs/FAST_INTENT_HEURISTICS_BOUNDARY.md)

## Allowed in `fast-intent-heuristics.*`

- Complexity tier routing (`read_only`, `compound`) via `CommandComplexityRouterService`
- Compound marker detection via `IntentDecompositionService`
- Structural command shape (list/show + appointments, upcoming scope, availability **routing** via `resolveAvailabilityIntentFromPrompt`)
- `paramHints` for re-rank (`complexityTier`, `useDecomposition`, structural flags)

## Forbidden in `fast-intent-heuristics.*`

- New paraphrase regex for **intent meaning** (acc-3.14)
- Imports from `ai-intent-heuristics`, `ai-intent-rescue`, `ai-semantic-intent`
- Symbols like `isFirstAvailableBookingPrompt`, `isTeamWideProviderAvailabilityQuery`, metric resolvers
- Bypassing LLM classify (phase 1 always runs classify; heuristics only feed re-rank)

## Where paraphrase goes

| Layer | When |
|-------|------|
| `AiSemanticIntentService` | Unknown/low-confidence classify; embedding match |
| `AiIntentRescueService` | Post-classify mislabel rescue |
| Semantic anchors + eval | New phrasing regression coverage |

## Before marking pipe-1.2 tasks done

```bash
cd backend && npm run test:pipe-fast-heuristics-boundary
cd backend && npm run test:pipe-understanding
```

Update `fast-intent-heuristics.boundary.ts` allowlist if adding a new **structural** delegation import.
